<spell-notebook "progress theming">
	<header level="1">
		Progress
		<header>A progress bar shows the progression of a task.</>
	</>
	<progress-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-progress-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every
			progress bar), or on the track through `::part(progress)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet
			reads each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. Style each bar with `::part(bar)` and its
			text with `::part(bar-text)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every progress bar on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-progress-radius: 999px;
			}
			/* one kind */
			ui-progress.slim {
			  --ui-progress-bar-height: 0.75em;
			}
			/* each bar */
			ui-progress.striped::part(bar) {
			  background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 0 0.5em, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.2) 0.5em 1em);
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				A `size` replaces the bar height, `inverted` the label colour, and `indicating` / `state` repaint the bar
				whatever `color` says. Never set the `--_ui-progress-*` / `--_progress-*` names: they're the sheet's private
				plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-progress" playground>
				<ui-progress value="74" bar-text="percent" aria-label="Standard"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
